    Call 1: ("Analyze output-buffer append and growth invariants around GrowOutputBuffer, SendBuffered, and CheckAvailableSize in wolfssl/src/internal.c. Is the correct robust fix to compact pending bytes from buffer + idx and reset idx in GrowOutputBuffer, and should CheckAvailableSize's capacity test also include idx to ensure growth/compaction whenever appending at idx + length would exceed bufferSize? Identify any callers that append at buffer + length rather than buffer + idx + length and implications of nonzero idx.", 'The supplied ASan report shows a partial send followed by WANT_WRITE leaves outputBuffer.idx > 0 and length equal to remaining bytes. DtlsMsgPoolSend calls CheckAvailableSize, which invokes GrowOutputBuffer. Current GrowOutputBuffer allocates size + length, copies length bytes from the old base, and leaves idx unchanged, so SendBuffered later reads length bytes at new buffer + stale idx beyond allocation. I have inspected wolfssl/src/internal.c:10071-10134, 9984-10066, and 10222-10270. Current CheckAvailableSize tests bufferSize - length < size, omitting idx, while at least the epoch-0 DtlsMsgPoolSend append at lines 8963-8966 explicitly writes at buffer + idx + length. The epoch-nonzero branch around line 9007 appears to write at buffer + length. I want the minimal root-cause patch preserving all expected buffer semantics, including static-memory allocator behavior where GrowOutputBuffer may return the same pointer.')...
